<title>USA: Equity Residential gets new line of credit.</title>
<headline>Equity Residential gets new line of credit.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equity Residential Properties Trust said Friday it obtained a new $250 million unsecured revolving line of credit underwritten and arranged by J.P. Morgan &amp; Co Inc and Bank of America Illinois.</p>
<p>Based on its current senior unsecured ratings, the borrowing cost is LIBOR plus 95 basis points, a reduction of 42.5 basis points from the company's previous line.</p>
<p>Equity Residential owns or has investments in 231 properties.  </p>
<p>The new three-year agreement replaces a credit agreement with Wells Fargo and Co and Bank of America.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
